The shaded region between $y=x+3$ and $y=3$ from $x=0$ to $x=2$ is rotated about the $x$-axis. Find the exact volume of the solid formed.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1.3cm, y=0.9cm]
\fill[gray!35] (0,3) -- plot[domain=0:2, samples=2, variable=\x] ({\x},{\x+3}) -- plot[domain=2:0, samples=2, variable=\x] ({\x},{3}) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-1.4,0) -- (3.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.4) -- (0,6.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-1.2:2.8, samples=2, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{\x+3});
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-1.3:2.9, samples=2, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{3});
\node at (1.05,5.6) {$y=x+3$};
\node at (2.4,2.35) {$y=3$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

The shaded region between $y=3x$ and $y=x$ from $x=0$ to $x=2$ is rotated about the $x$-axis. Find the exact volume of the solid formed.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1.3cm, y=0.7cm]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- plot[domain=0:2, samples=2, variable=\x] ({\x},{3*\x}) -- plot[domain=2:0, samples=2, variable=\x] ({\x},{\x}) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-1.4,0) -- (3.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-2.2) -- (0,7.6) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-0.7:2.4, samples=2, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{3*\x}) node[pos=0.90, above left] {$y=3x$};
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-1.2:2.9, samples=2, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{\x}) node[pos=0.95, below right] {$y=x$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

The shaded region enclosed by $y=6-x^{2}$ and $y=2$ is rotated about the $x$-axis. Find the exact volume of the solid formed.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.85cm, y=0.65cm]
\fill[gray!35] (-2,2) -- plot[domain=-2:2, samples=60, variable=\x] ({\x},{6-\x*\x}) -- plot[domain=2:-2, samples=2, variable=\x] ({\x},{2}) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-3.6,0) -- (3.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.8) -- (0,7.8) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-2.75:2.75, samples=60, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{6-\x*\x}) node[pos=0.42, above left] {$y=6-x^{2}$};
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-3.2:3.2, samples=2, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{2}) node[pos=0.95, above right] {$y=2$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

The shaded region enclosed by $y=3x$ and $y=x^{2}$ is rotated about the $y$-axis. Find the exact volume of the solid formed.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.95cm, y=0.5cm]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- plot[domain=0:3, samples=2, variable=\x] ({\x},{3*\x}) -- plot[domain=3:0, samples=60, variable=\x] ({\x},{\x*\x}) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-2.4,0) -- (4.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-2.4) -- (0,12.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-0.8:3.8, samples=2, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{3*\x});
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-2.3:3.4, samples=60, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{\x*\x});
\node at (1.1,6.2) {$y=3x$};
\node at (3.6,6.0) {$y=x^{2}$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

The shaded region enclosed by $y=x$ and $y=x^{3}$ for $x\ge 0$ is rotated about the $x$-axis. Find the exact volume of the solid formed.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=2cm, y=2cm]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- plot[domain=0:1, samples=2, variable=\x] ({\x},{\x}) -- plot[domain=1:0, samples=60, variable=\x] ({\x},{\x*\x*\x}) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-1.5,0) -- (1.7,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.5) -- (0,1.8) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-1.14:1.14, samples=60, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{\x*\x*\x}) node[pos=0.98, above left] {$y=x^{3}$};
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-1.4:1.4, samples=2, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{\x}) node[pos=0.99, below right] {$y=x$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

The shaded region between $y=2$ and $y=\dfrac{2}{x}$ from $x=1$ to $x=3$ is rotated about the $x$-axis. Find the exact volume of the solid formed.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1.2cm, y=1.2cm]
\fill[gray!35] (1,2) -- plot[domain=1:3, samples=2, variable=\x] ({\x},{2}) -- plot[domain=3:1, samples=60, variable=\x] ({\x},{2/\x}) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-0.6,0) -- (4.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.6) -- (0,3.6) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-0.4:4.2, samples=2, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{2});
\draw[thick, <->, domain=0.62:4.2, samples=80, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{2/\x});
\node at (3.6,2.45) {$y=2$};
\node at (3.7,1.1) {$y=\frac{2}{x}$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

The shaded region bounded by $y=\sqrt{x}$, $y=\sqrt{x-1}$ and the $x$-axis, from $x=0$ to $x=3$, is rotated about the $x$-axis. Find the exact volume of the solid formed.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1.2cm, y=1.4cm]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- plot[domain=0:1, samples=60, variable=\x] ({\x},{sqrt(\x)}) -- (1,0) -- cycle;
\fill[gray!35] (1,0) -- plot[domain=1:3, samples=60, variable=\x] ({\x},{sqrt(\x)}) -- plot[domain=3:1, samples=60, variable=\x] ({\x},{sqrt(\x-1)}) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-0.7,0) -- (4.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.7) -- (0,2.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick, ->, domain=0:4, samples=80, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{sqrt(\x)}) node[pos=0.80, above left] {$y=\sqrt{x}$};
\draw[thick, ->, domain=1:4, samples=80, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{sqrt(\x-1)}) node[pos=0.97, below right] {$y=\sqrt{x-1}$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]
